PhotoVault – Test Report
English UI · Light Mode

Version: Pre-launch MVP
Tester: Roger Sørqvist
Date: 2025-11-13

1. Overview

This report summarizes all functional issues, UI problems, untranslated text, missing features and inconsistencies discovered while testing PhotoVault in English language with Light Mode enabled.

Only actual findings are listed here – not the full test plan.

2. Home Page (English / Light Mode)
   Functional Issues

“See all (X)” does not apply filters

Example: Clicking See all (15) on Favorites opens Search Page without Favorites filter applied.

Recent uploads use scrollbar instead of navigation arrows

Scrollbar is slow and not smooth.

Recommended: left/right arrows or drag-scroll.

Visual & UI Issues

Very low contrast in Light Mode

Album names, count labels, and small UI elements are hard to see.

Favorite (heart) icons are barely visible in light theme.

i18n Issues

Several English strings still hardcoded:

“Recent uploads”

“See all”

“My albums”

Smart album labels

3. Album Page
   Functional Issues

Cover change (Set as cover) has no confirmation toast.

Moving photos to another album does not update UI

Changes visible only after full page refresh.

Collage Builder opened through Albums has major functionality gaps:

Stickers and text cannot be moved or repositioned.

Inconsistency: This is possible in the Photo Editor.

Visual Issues (Light Mode)

Text labels, dropdowns, and small buttons have insufficient contrast.

i18n Issues

Collage Builder layout names and instructions not translated (still hardcoded).

4. Collage Builder
   Critical Functional Gaps

No ability to move, resize or place text & stickers.

Makes the collage builder incomplete.

Expected: Drag-and-drop or X/Y sliders like Photo Editor.

i18n Issues

Hardcoded English strings:

“Select layout”

Layout names

Tips and descriptions

Empty state texts

Visual Issues

Low contrast in light mode across UI.

5. Search Page
   Functional Issues

“See All” from Home Page does not trigger pre-filtering.

No connection between sections and Search filters yet.

Visual Issues

Placeholder text and filter chips too faint in Light Mode.

i18n Issues

Missing translations for:

“Filters”

“Active filters”

“Clear”

Empty state text

Sorting labels

6. More Page / Settings
   Functional Issues

Admin Dashboard is missing a Back button.

Likely removed in a previous update.

Visual Issues

Low contrast on settings labels and icons.

i18n Issues

Some texts still hardcoded:

“Appearance”

“Light Mode”

“Storage”

“Language”

“Sign out”

7. Photo Editor
   General Notes

Core editor works fine.

Only minor Light Mode issues:

Low contrast on sliders and labels

Some adjustment names still hardcoded in English

8. Cross-App Issues (General)
   i18n (Major)

Large number of English strings not routed through i18n.

Both .json files need syncing for English/Norwegian parity.

Light Mode Contrast (Major)

Many UI elements too faint:
placeholders, labels, chips, icons, and small text across the app.

Navigation

Missing Back button in Admin Dashboard.

Some components behave differently across screens.

9. Prioritized Fix List
   Critical – Must Fix Before Launch

“See all (X)” not applying filters → Search Page integration.

Collage Builder missing text/sticker placement.

Light Mode contrast issues across app.

Admin Dashboard missing Back button.

Moving photos requires page refresh.

Important – Should Fix Before Launch

i18n issues: many untranslated strings.

Replace horizontal scrollbars with arrows on Home.

Collage Builder layout texts missing translation.

Missing toast after setting cover photo.

Nice to Have – Post Launch

Improved empty states.

Minor UI polishing in light mode.

10. Summary

The app is functionally solid and stable, but several UI and UX issues in Light Mode, i18n, and collage editing need to be addressed before release.
Overall, the English Light Mode test identifies clear areas for improvement and provides a solid base for the next iteration.
